Z||000036||Patrick's Dad||11-21-2001||11:44 AM||||Hmm....<P>Chicago did put on a great show.<P>Saw Rod Stewart in a small venue, not bad, almost caught a soccer ball, but had to rescue a friend from falling from the balcony.<P>O{+-&gt; was pretty amazing. What else can you say?<P>Saw Stryper twice, once even became temporary lighting crew!<P>Tom Jones; a performer I was working for opened for him.<P>Others: U2, Phil Collins, Amy Grant, Mariah, Take 6/Bobby McFerrin, Sheila E, Earth, Wind, and Fire, Kool & the Gang, Poison/Ratt/Great White, Bobby Brown (2d row + backstage pass), Al Jarreau, George Benson, Journey/Foriegner, David Bowie, Jr. Walker, Little Richard, Grover Washington.<P>Like to see: Creed (!!!), Staind and Shania.||||reg||1
Z||000037||Neal||11-21-2001||11:46 AM||||Green day<P>oddly enough, im not even a green day fan but they had the most entertainig show id ever seen by far...<BR>i think alot of it was because they play off the audience really well, they actually got some drunk guy on stage and hey was trying to play gituar  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000038||Lady Pegasus||11-21-2001||03:37 PM||||First, let me say some things.  Bif Naked is awesome.  Love her.  <BR>For the Styx fans..don't hate me, but remember the drummer that passed away?  I know his nephews.  So I can get front row tix and backstage passes when they come to town!!  Ok.<BR> <BR>I haven't been to MANY concerts, but this is my list....<BR>1996: First concert...Q101 Jamboree (That's a local radio station) Fifth row to SO many bands.  Sweet.<BR>1997: NO DOUBT!!!  I LOVE THEM!!  Gwen is SO hot.  If I was a dude....anyhow<BR>1998: Metallica  Pretty sweet show.  INTERESTING crowd.  Almost got kicked in the head by a crowd surfer.  Fun.<BR>2000: Free concert.  Not too thrilling.<BR>2001: Free concert at the House Of Blues with Poe.  Another one of my favs!!   She rocked out.  I even got to meet her after the show.  She is SO sweet and beautuiful.<BR>2001: Tori Amos.  Oh my god.  I died and went to heaven.  Tori is so beautiful and talented.  Imagine being able to play a piano and a harpsichord at the same time, but playing two seperate melodies.  Oh my god.  I was in heaven.  She came out and did three encores.  I love her.<BR>I am hoping to catch Poe, Tori and No Doubt (new album coming out December 11!!) next time each of them comes to town.  Other than that, I'm broke...so not too many concerts here.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Hey pretty....don't you wanna take a ride with me...through my world?||||reg||1
